          "type": "turn",
          "question": "When someone says they have heart failure, does that mean the heart has stopped working?",
          "answer": "Heart failure is a clinical syndrome where the heart cannot fill with or pump out enough blood to meet the body's needs at normal filling pressures. The name can be misleading; it does not mean that the heart has stopped working or is about to stop. Instead, it is a chronic condition that is often managed for many years, as described in the \"Heart failure\" document.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
